"""
1D vertical (heave) buoyancy + gravity for a floating ship hull.

Decoupled from the planar `Hull3DOF` surge/sway/yaw dynamics — this runs as a separate
1D state in the vertical direction. ShipSIM makes the same split: `HidrodynamicXYY`
handles planar dynamics, and `HidrodynamicZRP` handles vertical / roll / pitch. We can't
do full ZRP without 3D multibody, but a 1D heave model captures the essential physics
(gravity vs. buoyancy, hydrostatic restoring force, draft as a function of mass).

States:
- `z` — vertical position [m], positive *up*, with z = 0 at the calm waterline
- `w` — heave velocity = der(z)

Volume model (simplified, linear in draft via the block coefficient):
```math
V_\\mathrm{submerged} = C_b \\cdot L_{pp} \\cdot B \\cdot \\mathrm{draft}
```
with `draft = max(-z, 0)`.

Equations of motion:
```math
\\dot z = w
```
```math
m \\dot w = -m g + \\rho_\\mathrm{sea} V_\\mathrm{submerged} g - D_z w + F_{z,\\mathrm{extra}}
```

At equilibrium, `m·g = ρ·V·g` gives `draft_eq = m / (ρ·C_b·L·B)`, which is used as the
default initial condition so the model starts at rest.

Limitations:
- Block-coefficient volume is *linear* in draft; for moderate excursions around
  equilibrium this is a reasonable proxy for the waterplane × Δdraft behavior.
- When the hull rises above the waterline (draft = 0), buoyancy goes to zero — i.e.
  the ship is in free fall (sensible).
- No roll / pitch coupling (would need a multi-DOF block).
- No wave model: caller drives `Fz_extra` to inject wave forcing.

Pair this with `Hull3DOF` (planar) for a 4-DOF maneuvering + heave model. Both
components share the same `mass` parameter conceptually but their DOFs are orthogonal,
so they don't directly couple in equations.
"""
component Buoyancy1D
  parameter mass::Mass = 5e6
  parameter Lpp::Length = 100
  parameter B::Length = 20
  parameter Cb::Real = 0.693
  parameter rho_sea::Density = 1025
  parameter g::Acceleration = 9.80665
  "Linear heave damping coefficient [N·s/m] (≥ 0)"
  parameter Dz::Real = 1e6

  "External vertical force [N], up-positive (e.g. wave force, cargo loading)"
  Fz_extra = RealInput()

  "Vertical position [m], up-positive, z = 0 at calm waterline"
  z = RealOutput()
  "Heave velocity [m/s]"
  w = RealOutput()
  "Hull depth below waterline [m] (≥ 0)"
  draft = RealOutput()
  "Displaced volume [m³]"
  V_submerged = RealOutput()

  variable z_state::Length
  variable w_state::Velocity
  variable F_buoy::Force
relations
  initial w_state = 0
  # Initial position = equilibrium draft = mass / (ρ·Cb·L·B) below waterline.
  initial z_state = -mass / (rho_sea * Cb * Lpp * B)

  z = z_state
  w = w_state
  der(z_state) = w_state

  draft = ifelse(z_state < 0, -z_state, 0)
  V_submerged = Cb * Lpp * B * draft
  F_buoy = rho_sea * V_submerged * g

  mass * der(w_state) = -mass * g + F_buoy - Dz * w_state + Fz_extra
end
